{
  "schema": "earthsciio/scenario/v1",
  "id": "esm-sources",
  "description": "Building a provider from an esm data_sources entry (spec/esm-sources.md section 3). Each case passes `entry` (named `name`) and `options` (variables, substitutions, url_override, window_s) to the track's constructor. A case with `error` fails with that code in the message, and every `mentions` string. Otherwise the provider has `format`, is CONST iff `const`, has `time_dim`, `refresh_times_s` over window_s, and at each `files[].t_s` reads record `record` of the file at `file_anchor_s` whose primary URL is `url` and whose mirrors are `mirrors`. `samples` are read offline from the corpus cache (blobs of the calendar-cadence scenario), with `records_per_sample` as given, the arrays nested in file dimension order.",
